# Case of the Pilfered Proof: "Whenever a Detective you control ... is turned face up, put a +1/+1 counter on it." (CR 701.40b, 701.58, 122.1). With the Case out, Bot1's Cryptic Coat
# cloaks the top card of its library, a Novice Inspector, face down as a 2/2 with no subtypes: a face-down permanent is no Detective, so nothing happens as it enters. Turned face up
# for its mana cost, {W}, it is a Human Detective, 1/2, and the Case puts a +1/+1 counter on it. With the Coat's +1/+0 it is a 3/3.

